# Checks: the order of a script's problems (issue #37). Skript reads every structure's header first (options,
# variables, using, headers it can't understand), then function headers, then functions, events and commands, as it
# loads them by priority, and a command entry by entry.

options:
	good: 1
	bad option line

on load:
	frob one

on frobnicate the wibble:
	broadcast "x"

function message_order_a(n: number) :: number:
	frob two
	return 1

command /messageorderc:
	permission message: hi
	cooldown: frob seconds
	cooldown message: "%frob nonsense%"
	cooldown bypass: x.y
	trigger:
		frob three
	usage: "%frob usage%"

variables:
	{message_order::a} = frob value
	this is not a variable line

function message_order_b(n: numberz):
	broadcast "x"

using frobfeature

every frob seconds:
	broadcast "x"

on chat:
	frob four
	if 1 is 1:
		broadcast "x"

function message_order_c() :: number:
	frob five
	return 1
